    Fix abort for registered STARTING jobs (#4904)
    
    ### Description
    
    Addresses FLARE-3039 by allowing a client abort request to proceed when
    a launched job is registered in the `STARTING` state. In that state,
    `JobExecutor` terminates the stored launcher handle immediately instead
    of trying to send an in-band abort to a worker that has not reported
    `STARTED`.
    
    The persisted `STARTING` state was introduced after the older abort
    guards, so those guards acknowledged abort requests without acting on
    them during this window. This change allows launcher-managed runtimes,
    including queued jobs, to be canceled while preserving the existing
    graceful shutdown path for `STARTED` jobs.
